{
  "name": "AKUH organises trauma course",
  "parent_id": 203313630673674,
  "group_id": "db49f969-ca0d-4ee7-ade4-a4096455827d",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-30T15:09:21.790Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-08-12T14:55:20.734Z",
  "published_at": "2026-08-12T14:55:20.720Z",
  "id": 203712765136950,
  "uuid": "2ab3ff21-6b5a-4d9f-9ef0-26054884e6dc",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "9d9e7282-fd2f-a750-1dec-7d5154d6405d",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "43b7c106-e8ce-0af4-bc15-e6ce700b4c7e",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Appropriate management in the early hours can significantly reduce the associated deaths and disabilities. In order to achieve this, it is important that doctors and paramedical staff who are involved in the management of trauma patients should be well trained in the initial handling and care.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "With this aim, Aga Khan University Hospital (AKUH) has started awareness and training programmes for health care providers. \"Unfortunately in developing countries, very little attention has been given at any level to improve the management of victims who most of the time are young healthy individuals and may be the only bread earners of the family,\" said Dr. Muhammad Qamarul Hoda, Course Director, and Associate Professor, Department of Anaesthesia, AKUH. He said that by improving trauma care in the \"golden hour\", mortality could be reduced which would not only benefit the victims and their families but also be of great benefit to the nation.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The three-day intensive course consisted of pre and post-course test, core content lectures, interactive case presentation and discussions on simulated patients, video-assisted learning, hands-on  life saving procedures on manikins and anaesthetized animals, and a final performance proficiency evaluation followed by certification of successful candidates.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The ceremony was also opportune for the launch of a \"trauma manual\" that covers important trauma related topics written by national and international authors of related fields. This manual was also given to the participants of the course and is available for all health care providers.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The ceremony also included a short film on the current state of management of trauma patient in our country which needs to be changed.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
